&Q000528 = A prayer for Samsu-iluna (Samsu-iluna E)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.8.3.5
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.8.3.5&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. [X X] X-ŋu₁₀ mu gi₁₆-sa saŋ il₂-la me-te nam-nun-na
#lem: X; X; X; mu[name]; gilsa[treasure]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; mete[appropriate thing]; namnun[magnificence]
#tr.en: My …… of eternal fame, head lifted high in princely worth, 
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. [X X] X niŋ₂-si-sa₂ niŋ₂-gen₆-e ki aŋ₂-e
#lem: X; X; X; niŋsisa[justice]; niŋgina[truth]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: …… who loves righteousness and truth, 
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. [...] X-e mu mah sa₄-a
#lem: X; X; mu[name]; mah[great]; še[call by name]
#tr.en: …… named with an august name, 
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. {[d]}[en]-lil₂-le X X nam gal tar X-a
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; X; X; nam[fate]; gal[big]; tar[cut]; X
#tr.en: for whom @wDN{Enlil} …… has determined a great destiny, 
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. {d}nin-lil₂-le X [...]
#lem: Ninlil[1]DN; X; X
#tr.en: and @wDN{Ninlil} ……! The valiant @wDN{Ninurta} is your helper. 
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. {d}nin-urta kalag-<ga> a₂-tah-zu i₃-me-a
#lem: Ninurtak[1]DN; kalag[strong]; atah[helper]; me[be]
#tr.en: In the @wTN{E-kur}, @wDN{Nuska} the august minister of @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. {d}nuska sukkal-mah {d}en-lil₂-la₂ kingal kur-kur-ra
#lem: Nuska[1]DN; sukkalmah[an official]; Enlil[1]DN; kingal[an official]; kur[mountain(s)]
#tr.en: the assembly leader of all lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. e₂-kur-ra ad-da saŋ e₂-gal-la-zu i₃-me-a
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; adda[father]; saŋ[head]; egal[palace]; me[be]
#tr.en: is your foremost palace superintendent. 
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. nam-til₃-la gu₂ an-še₃ he₂-ni-zig₃
#lem: namtil[life]; gu[neck]; an[sky]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: Throughout your life, 
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. nam-nun-na saŋ an-še₃ he₂-ni-il₂
#lem: namnun[magnificence]; saŋ[head]; an[sky]; il[raise]
#tr.en: may you carry your neck high; 
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. sa-am-su-i-lu-na me-te nam-nun-na
#lem: Samsuʾiluna[01]; mete[appropriate thing]; namnun[magnificence]
#tr.en: in princely manner may you lift your head high! 
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. nam-til₃-la ud-bi su₃-ud-ba-ni-ib
#lem: namtil[life]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]
#tr.en: -- Prolong the days of his life for @wRN{@wDN{Samsu}-iluna}, of princely worth! 
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. igi sag₉-ga an lugal diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄ he₂-e-ši-bar
#lem: igi[eye]; sag[good]; An[1]DN; lugal[king]; diŋir[deity]; bar[place outside]
#tr.en: May @wDN{An}, king of the gods, look upon you favourably; 
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. an gal mah a-a diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄
#lem: An[1]DN; gal[big]; mah[great]; aya[father]; diŋir[deity]
#tr.en: the great and august @wDN{An}, the father of the gods, 
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. aga su-lim si mah gal gur₃-ru
#lem: aga[tiara]; sulim[awesome radiance]; simuš[brilliance]; mah[great]; gal[big]; gur[lift]
#tr.en: he with the splendid crown, full of great and august radiance, 
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. {ŋiš}gu-za nam-lugal-la pa mul-bi daŋal-la an-gin₇ DU X
#lem: guza[chair]; namlugal[kingship]; pa[branch]; mul[shine]; daŋal[wide]; an[sky]; X; X
#tr.en: …… your royal throne whose branches and sprouts …… as wide as the sky. 
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. PA ka-aš bar [...] X X X si sa₂-sa₂-e
#lem: X; kaš[decision]; bar[place outside]; X; X; X; X; si[horn]; sa[equal]
#tr.en: May he bestow upon you, during the days of your long life, 
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. saŋ gig₂ zi-ŋal₂ a-na lu-a u₂-a-še₃ lah₅-lah₅-e
#lem: saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; ziŋal[living things]; ana[what?]; lu[abundant]; ua[provisioner]; lah[plural stem of tum ⟦bring⟧]
#tr.en: the power to make decisions ……, to direct ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. ud til₃-la su₃-ra₂-še₃ saŋ-e-eš hu-mu-<ni>-in-rig₇
#lem: ud[sun]; til[live (of a single person)]; sud[distant]; saŋ[head]; rig[donate]
#tr.en: to serve as the provider of the black-headed creatures in all their multitude! 
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. {d}en-lil₂ X X lugal kur-kur-ra-ke₄
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; X; X; lugal[king]; kur[mountain(s)]
#tr.en: May @wDN{Enlil}, ……, the king of all countries, 
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. niŋ₂-dug₄-ga X X a₂ bad-a-zu he₂-ri-DU
#lem: niŋduga[speech]; X; X; a[arm]; bad[open]; X
#tr.en: protect you …… command. 
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. iri ma-da-za hu-mu-ra-ab-X
#lem: iri[city]; mada[land]; X
#tr.en: May he …… for you the city of your country. 
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. suhuš ma-da hu-mu-ra-ab-gen₆-ne₂
#lem: suhuš[foundation]; mada[land]; gin[confirm]
#tr.en: May he make firm for you the foundation of your country. 
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. {d}nin-lil₂ nin diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄
#lem: Ninlil[1]DN; nin[lady]; diŋir[deity]
#tr.en: May @wDN{Ninlil}, the queen of deities, 
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. šag₄ hul₂-la-ni-ta he₂-mu-e-ši-ib₂-RI
#lem: šag[heart]; hul[rejoice]; X
#tr.en: joyfully …… for you, 
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. saŋ-ki zalag-ga-na igi hu-mu-ri-gub
#lem: saŋki[forehead]; zalag[bright]; igi[eye]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: and may she look upon you with shining face; 
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. ki {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ta ad gi₄-gi₄-da# X
#lem: ki[place]; Enlil[1]DN; ad[voice]; gi[turn]; X
#tr.en: may she who takes counsel …… with @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. ki SI X en₃# tar-tar-re-da X
#lem: ki[place]; X; X; en[cvne]; tar[cut]; X
#tr.en: and who cares for ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. inim sag₉-sag₉-ga X UŠ he₂-X
#lem: inim[word]; sag[good]; X; X; X
#tr.en: …… her favourable word. 
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. {d}nin-urta ur-saŋ kalag-ga {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ke₄
#lem: Ninurtak[1]DN; ursaŋ[warrior]; kalag[strong]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: May @wDN{Ninurta}, the strong warrior of @wDN{Enlil}, the lord of decisions, 
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. en eš-bar an {d}en-lil₂-gin₇ dug₄-ga mah-a-ni dugud-da
#lem: en[lord]; ešbar[decision]; An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; dug[speak]; mah[great]; dugud[heavy]
#tr.en: whose august commands are as weighty as those of @wDN{An} and @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. nam-nir-ŋal₂ me-lem₄ nam-ur-saŋ gaba-ŋal₂ lu₂-u ru-gu₂
#lem: namnirŋal[authority]; melim[frightening splendor]; namursaŋ[heroism]; gabaŋal[forceful]; lu[person]; rugu[withstand]
#tr.en: he of lordly character, terrifying splendour and heroism, who resists the forceful, 
#etcsl: line-id=32

33. sipad!(|PA.KU|) kalag-ga hul-ŋal₂ erim₂ gaz-gaz{ka-e-eš}
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; kalag[strong]; huluŋal[evil]; erim[enemy]; gaz[kill]
#tr.en: the strong shepherd (?) who crushes the evil and wicked -- may he spread out in heaps for you the inhabitants of the cities which you hate, 
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. iri gu₂ du₃-a-zu zar-gin₇ ha-ra-ab-sal-e
#lem: iri[city]; gu[neck]; du[build]; zar[sheaf (of barley)]; sal[thin]
#tr.en: and may he deliver your enemies into your hands! May @wDN{Nuska}, 
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. erim₂-ŋal₂-zu šu-zu-še₃ he₂-bi₂-ib-si-si
#lem: erimŋal[wicked]; šu[hand]; si[fill]
#tr.en: the august minister of @wDN{Enlil}, let you enter brick-built @wTN{E-kur} joyfully with your offerings, 
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. {d}nuska sukkal-mah {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ke₄
#lem: Nuska[1]DN; sukkalmah[an official]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: and escort you before the shining faces of @wDN{Enlil} and @wDN{Ninlil}; 
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. kadra-zu šeg₁₂ e₂-kur-ra-še₃ hul₂-la he-ni-ib-ku₄-ku₄#
#lem: kadra[greeting gift]; šeg[brick]; Ekur[1]TN; hul[rejoice]; kur[enter]
#tr.en: in @wSN{Babylon}, the city of heroes, 
#etcsl: line-id=37

38. saŋ-ki zalag-ga {d}en-lil₂ {d}nin-<lil₂>-la₂-ke₄ an-ta he₂-bi₂-ib-gi₄-gi₄-in
#lem: saŋki[forehead]; zalag[bright]; Enlil[1]DN; Ninlil[1]DN; an[sky]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: may he make firm for you the foundation of your kingship. 
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. babilim₂{ki} iri ur-saŋ-e-ne-ka
#lem: Babilim[1]; iri[city]; ursaŋ[warrior]
#tr.en: The august command …… @wDN{Enlil} ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. nam-lugal-zu suhuš-bi ha-ra-ab-gen₆-ne₂
#lem: namlugal[kingship]; suhuš[foundation]; gin[confirm]
#tr.en: ……, may …… be their king! 
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. inim mah dug₄-ga X {d}en-lil₂ X [...]
#lem: inim[word]; mah[great]; dug[speak]; X; Enlil[1]DN; X; X
#tr.en: ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. [...] X lugal-bi he₂-a
#lem: X; X; lugal[king]; me[be]
#tr.en: may he …… a place for you! 
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. [...] X X ki ha-ra-ab-sa₂-sa₂
#lem: X; X; X; ki[place]; sa[equal]
#tr.en: ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=43

44. [...] X X AN ud-gin₇ an kug-ga itid-da u₃-tud-da#
#lem: X; X; X; X; ud[sun]; an[sky]; kug[pure]; itud[moon]; utud[give birth (to)]
#tr.en: like the light born monthly in the pure sky. 
#etcsl: line-id=44

45. [...] X X-e nam-til₃-da gurun gibil-gin₇ he₂#-en-da-mu₂-mu₂
#lem: X; X; X; namtil[life]; gurun[fruit]; gibil[new]; mu[grow]
#tr.en: ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=45

46. [sa-am]-su#-i-lu-na lugal-ŋu₁₀
#lem: Samsuʾiluna[01]; lugal[king]
#tr.en: and may you too grow throughout your life like a fresh fruit, O @wRN{@wDN{Samsu}-iluna}, my king! 
#etcsl: line-id=46







